  "lesson": {
    "title": "Preguntas WH con do/does",
    "rule": "Para preguntar por información usa una palabra WH + do/does + sujeto + verbo: Where do you work? / What does she do? WH más usadas: what (qué), where (dónde), when (cuándo), who (quién), why (por qué), how (cómo). Con he/she/it usamos 'does' y el verbo sin -s: What does she do? (no 'does she does').",
    "examples": [
      "What is your name?",
      "Where do you work?",
      "When do you finish?",
      "Who is your friend?",
      "How much is this?"
    ],
    "commonMistakes": [
      "Where you work? → Where do you work?",
      "What does she does? → What does she do?",
      "How much cost? → How much is it?"
    ]
  },
  "pronunciationTip": "Las preguntas WH bajan la entonación al final: Where do you work? (el 'work' baja, no sube).",
